usbdrv - third-party components and licenses
============================================

usbdrv does not include or link any third-party code. It runs the following programs as separate
processes, only if the user supplies them:

1. libwdi / wdi-simple.exe  (https://github.com/pbatard/libwdi)
   License: GNU LGPL v3 or later (library and examples/wdi-simple.c).
   Role: builds the INF + catalog, signs it with a self-signed certificate, installs the driver.
   Copyright (c) 2010-2023 Pete Batard and other contributors (see AUTHORS in the libwdi source).
   Version checked: v1.5.1, commit 9b23b82a2dd1cbffc16d46c212f92c6bf8c0c602.
   Source: https://github.com/pbatard/libwdi
   Not distributed in this repository: it is fetched and built by the user
   (docs/building-wdi-simple.md). The texts of the LGPL-3.0 and of the GPL-3.0 it refers to are in
   LICENSES/.
   If you redistribute a wdi-simple.exe binary, the LGPL obligations apply to that binary (license
   text, notice, corresponding source, way to rebuild it): use scripts/package_wdi_bundle.py, which
   refuses to build the bundle unless all of it is there. See docs/licenza.md section 4.

2. Windows components called by name: PowerShell, pnputil.exe, setupapi.dev.log. Part of Windows.

Not used, not copied: Zadig (examples/zadig.c, GNU GPL v3 or later). Its behaviour was studied only to
document which features usbdrv offers (docs/zadig-features.md).

Driver binaries that libwdi may embed when YOU build it (not in this repository). Licenses checked on
2026-10-13, details and SHA-256 in docs/embedded-drivers.txt:
  * WinUSB co-installers from the Windows Driver Kit 8.0: Microsoft Windows Driver Frameworks 1.11 terms
    (redistribution allowed with conditions, including an indemnity toward Microsoft).
  * libusb-win32 1.4.0.0: driver libusb0.sys under the GPL, library and installer under the LGPL.
  * libusbK 3.1.0.0: dual license, New BSD or GPL.
  * usbser: in-box Windows driver, not redistributed.
Run 'usbdrv licenses' to print this list. Before distributing a binary, list only the drivers it really
contains (docs/embedded-drivers.txt) and follow docs/licenza.md section 4.

